p = 3 (excluded by hp3): of 600 random families, S0' read with p = 3 would be false for 600 (some signing has unequal class sums); S1' with p = 3, i = 1 false for 190 of 190 families whose level 1 is not live; S2' false for 600 (every family with a nonempty pivot set).  Examples: {'S0': (1, 5, [4, 0, 0, 2, 10, 9, 7]), 'S2': (1, 5, [4, 0, 0, 2, 10, 9, 7], 2), 'S1': (1, 2, [4, 5, 5, 2, 5])}
   with 'remainder modulo Phi_(3^i d) divisible by 3' as the hypothesis instead: 698 such signings, 0 of them not flat
